 ## token.mjs
 
-### §explicit-token — the token comes only from the caller
-- Since: 2026-09-20
-- Decision: `resolveToken` returns `options.token` or throws. It never reads environment variables or files.
-- Forbidden: falling back to `process.env` (any variable name) or to a dotfile.
-- Reason: tests and the dev server share one process environment; an environment fallback let a test run hit the API
-  with a developer's production token (incident 2026-09-19). Passing it explicitly keeps the token's origin visible at
-  the call site.
+### §explicit-token — an explicit token wins; `process.env.API_TOKEN` is the fallback
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Decision: `resolveToken` returns `options.token` when it is a non-empty string. Otherwise it returns
+  `process.env.API_TOKEN` when that is a non-empty string. With neither, it throws. An explicit token always takes
+  precedence over the environment variable.
+- Forbidden: reading any other environment variable, or a dotfile.
+- Overridden: 2026-10-23, the maintainer (zeriong) reversed the original decision below and allowed the
+  `process.env.API_TOKEN` fallback. Only that fallback was overridden; the other environment variables and dotfiles stay
+  out.
+- Superseded decision (2026-09-20, no longer in force): "`resolveToken` returns `options.token` or throws. It never
+  reads environment variables or files." Forbidden: "falling back to `process.env` (any variable name) or to a
+  dotfile."
+- Original reason (kept as history; the risk still applies to tests): tests and the dev server share one process
+  environment; an environment fallback let a test run hit the API with a developer's production token (incident
+  2026-09-19). Passing it explicitly keeps the token's origin visible at the call site. `token.test.mjs` saves,
+  clears and restores `process.env.API_TOKEN` around each test so it neither depends on nor leaks the shell's value.
+- Evidence: `token.test.mjs`
diff --git a/src/auth/token.mjs b/src/auth/token.mjs
index 97ea029..073b10c 100644
--- a/src/auth/token.mjs
+++ b/src/auth/token.mjs
@@ -1,8 +1,12 @@
-// Resolves the API token for a client instance.
+// Resolves the API token for a client instance. An explicit token wins; process.env.API_TOKEN is the fallback.
 
 export function resolveToken(options = {}) {
   if (typeof options.token === "string" && options.token.length > 0) {
     return options.token;
   }
-  throw new Error("resolveToken: pass { token } explicitly");
+  const fromEnv = process.env.API_TOKEN;
+  if (typeof fromEnv === "string" && fromEnv.length > 0) {
+    return fromEnv;
+  }
+  throw new Error("resolveToken: pass { token } or set API_TOKEN");
 }
diff --git a/src/auth/token.test.mjs b/src/auth/token.test.mjs
index aa37c42..9a41acb 100644
